<example type="alternative">
# API Reference

## Authentication

Authentication uses JWT tokens passed in the Authorization header:

```http
GET /api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
```

> ⚠️ **Warning:** Never share your authentication tokens.

### Error Responses

Errors follow this structure:

| Status | Meaning             |
|:-------|:--------------------|
| 401    | Unauthorized        |
| 403    | Forbidden           |
| 404    | Resource not found  |
</example>
</examples>

<critical_points>
- ALWAYS include a single level-1 heading as the document title
- NEVER skip heading levels in document hierarchy
- SPECIFY language in code blocks for proper syntax highlighting
- USE consistent formatting for similar elements across documentation
- ADD blank lines before and after block elements for readability
- INCLUDE proper alignment indicators in tables
- MAINTAIN a clean and consistent indentation style
- FORMAT Mermaid diagrams with descriptive labels and comments
- TEST documentation rendering in the target environment
- CLOSE XML tags on their own line at the parent indentation level
</critical_points>